    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d941">

                <pb facs="1095" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg999"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New London,
                                Conn.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-07-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your telegram of the 22d
                    instant sanctioning the expenditure of money for the relief of United States
                    citizens at Habana, I have the honor to inform you that Her Majesty’s acting
                    consul-general at Habana has drawn upon you for the sum of $500.</p>
                <p>Mr. Jerome adds that the $2,000 which he is authorized to draw will be sufficient
                    for some time to come.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
